    "details": {
      "description": "<p>A budget-grade, open-cockpit loader frame of the kind found in cargo bays, dockyards, and scrap yards across Terminus and Traverse ports. The operator straps into a harness between two hydraulic arms, each ending in a heavy three-finger clamp rated for shifting crates, hull plating, and engine components. It was never designed for combat, but a clamp that can peel a bulkhead can peel armor just as easily.</p><p>The exposed actuators and power bus make it vulnerable to overload discharges.</p>",
      "level": {
        "value": 3
      },
